The GPUI front-end's SDK-CONSUMING half: the renderer-free shell (PLAT-20).

This whole tree is a declared Embed SDK consumer, the same directory-marker
spelling `src/frontend/tui/app/` and `src/frontend/headless_app/` already use,
and for the same reason: marking each file would be noise and being a consumer
is the point rather than an accident of where the code landed.

PLAT-20's shell/leaf decomposition is what this marker enforces. The milestone
asks for *"the shell is `HeadlessApp` plus the layout model, and only the leaves
are GPUI"*, and *"a shell that needed changing to host a second GPU front-end
was not renderer-free"* is its verification gate. Neither sentence is checkable
by review. This marker makes the outward half checkable: every module beneath
it may reach `codetracer_embed`, `headless_app` and `isonim`, and a reach past
the facade is a build-and-gate failure rather than a note.

`src/frontend/gpui/host/` is deliberately NOT covered, exactly as
`src/frontend/tui/host/` is not: it is the only part of this front-end allowed
to spawn a `replay-server` and open a local recording. The exemption is the
absence of a marker, and `ci/test/sdk-facade-boundary.sh` asserts both halves
for the terminal front-end; the same shape here is why the two front-ends can be
read against each other.
